  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, all design choices are uncertain. The most informative first experiment is a standard, moderate multimodal baseline that anchors the design space for all future comparisons. config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) uses well-understood, standard components at each dimension: PCA for RNA (simple, fast, no training), ResNet-50 for image (standard pretrained backbone), avgpool for aggregation (simple, interpretable), and concat for fusion (simple, no learned weights). This places it near the center of the configuration space, so every subsequent experiment—varying RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt), image encoder (ViT-L), aggregation (transformer), fusion (weighted), profile setting (singleprofile), or modality (rna_only/image_only)—constitutes a clean single-variable comparison against this baseline. Starting with the simplest reasonable multimodal pipeline also lets us determine whether the basic architecture is functional before investing budget in more complex encoders or fusion strategies, maximizing the information gained per experiment under the limited budget."
}

